From d54eca1a8c3e38cc0a0dd6d8ee24d58ac4ddef6f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Revulate <76570121+Revulate@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:33:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf(gpui): patch animated image frames into the presented
 scene

Animated content that changes only its frame no longer needs a window
redraw. `Window::paint_animated_image` paints an image as a keyed slot;
cached views carry their slots when replayed, and each slot is resolved
to its sprite once the scene is sorted. `Window::patch_animated_image`
then swaps that sprite's atlas tile in the presented scene and in the
paint operation cached views replay, records the sprite's bounds as
damage and requests a present-only frame. It refuses (returns false)
when the key was not painted, was painted twice, or a draw is running.

The Direct3D 11 renderer presents patch-only frames with
`IDXGISwapChain1::Present1` dirty rectangles. Every frame still redraws
the whole back buffer; the rectangles only let the compositor update
less. The first present after resize or device recovery is full.

`Window::frame_stage_statistics` reports cumulative CPU time per frame
stage (layout, prepaint, paint, scene ordering, renderer upload, encode
and the swap-chain present call), views rendered and reused, presents,
partial presents, patches and patch refusals by reason.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
